## 9. Backup & Recovery

### 9.1 Backup Location

**Primary:** Local storage on mini PC (same physical disk as production)

**Rationale:** Physical ownership, no cloud costs. Full-disk encryption (LUKS) protects against physical theft.

**Risk Accepted:** Single point of failure. If disk dies, both production and backup lost.

**Mitigation:** 
- High-quality SSD
- SMART monitoring for disk health
- Git content backup (offsite for content only)

### 9.2 Backup Schedule

| Type | Frequency | Method |
|------|-----------|--------|
| Database | Nightly 2:00 AM | `VACUUM INTO` |
| Media | Nightly 2:30 AM | rsync |
| Full system | Weekly Sunday 3:00 AM | tar |
| Git content | On publish | git push |

### 9.3 Backup Implementation

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# backup.sh - Runs nightly

DATE=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
BACKUP_DIR=/backups

# Database backup (safe method)
sqlite3 /var/www/site/data/site.db "VACUUM INTO '$BACKUP_DIR/db/site-$DATE.db';"

# Media backup
rsync -av --delete /var/www/site/public/uploads/ $BACKUP_DIR/media/

# Cleanup old backups (30 days)
find $BACKUP_DIR/db/ -name "*.db" -mtime +30 -delete
find $BACKUP_DIR/media/ -mtime +30 -delete

# Weekly full system (Sunday only)
if [ $(date +%u) -eq 7 ]; then
    tar -czf $BACKUP_DIR/system/system-$DATE.tar.gz \
        /var/www/site/ \
        /etc/nginx/ \
        /etc/systemd/system/
    find $BACKUP_DIR/system/ -mtime +90 -delete
fi
```

