## 15. Decision Rationale

### 15.1 Two-Factor Authentication (New)

**Decision:** Include TOTP 2FA for admin

**Rationale:**
- Single admin account holds client PII
- Password alone is vulnerable to reuse/guessing
- TOTP adds minimal friction (6-digit code from phone)
- PIPEDA compliance benefits
- Backup codes prevent lockout

### 15.2 Backup: Local Only (New)

**Decision:** Backups stored on same physical disk

**Rationale:**
- Zero ongoing costs
- Physical ownership of all data
- LUKS full-disk encryption protects against theft
- Risk accepted: single point of failure
- Mitigated by SMART monitoring + Git content backup

### 15.3 Privacy Policy: Dedicated Page (Revised)

**Decision:** Privacy policy as dedicated public page

**Rationale:**
- Legal compliance requires accessibility
- Always visible in footer
- Not hidden by default
- Editable content in admin

### 15.4 Magic Link Two-Step (New)

**Decision:** Two-step magic link flow (GET landing + POST consume)

**Rationale:**
- Email security scanners (Outlook SafeLinks, Gmail prefetch) automatically follow links
- If GET consumes token, scanners burn it before client sees email
- Landing page requires explicit user action
- Standard pattern for email-based authentication

### 15.5 Global Announcement Rename (Revised)

**Decision:** Rename "All-Hands" to "Global Announcement"

**Rationale:**
- "All-Hands" is corporate jargon
- "Global Announcement" is clearer for travel clients
- Better UX for non-technical users

### 15.6 Email Queue (New)

**Decision:** Asynchronous email queue

**Rationale:**
- Prevents API timeouts with many recipients
- Handles Resend rate limits gracefully
- Retry logic for failed sends
- Better observability

